('aca0ee51-f65f-5677-a436-0b8f350b207f', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 33, 33, 'The mean of an alternating current over a cycle is zero, yet it heats a resistor. Why?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Heating depends on I², which is positive for either direction of current', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = I²R ≥ 0 at every instant. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: P ∝ I². C1: always positive. A1: D (Heating depends on I², which is positive for either direction of current).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('b9292727-0119-564b-bb8d-075e01fb0aa7', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 34, 34, 'An a.c. supply has an r.m.s. voltage of 12 V and drives an r.m.s. current of 0.50 A through a resistor. Calculate the peak power.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '12', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Mean power = 12 × 0.50 = 6.0 W. Peak power = 2 × 6.0 = 12 W. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: P = V_rms I_rms. C1: peak = 2 × mean. A1: P₀ = 12 W.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('0d057a8c-593a-56cc-a6aa-388b83177e7e', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 35, 35, 'A 50 V r.m.s. supply drives a sinusoidal current of peak 1.5 A through a resistor. Calculate its resistance.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '47.14', 'Ω', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'I_rms = 1.5 ÷ √2 = 1.06 A. R = 50 ÷ 1.061 = 47.1 Ω. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: I_rms. C1: R = V_rms/I_rms. A1: R = 47.1 Ω.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('3cb0736b-0253-5683-82d3-c6a3bfe6c2da', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 36, 36, 'Which describes a graph of I² against time for a sinusoidal current of peak I₀?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It oscillates between 0 and I₀² at twice the supply frequency, with a mean of I₀²/2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'sin² ωt = ½(1 − cos 2ωt). Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: always positive. C1: double frequency. C1: mean I₀²/2. A1: B (It oscillates between 0 and I₀² at twice the supply frequency, with a mean of I₀²/2).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('5f7e2d7d-9c6c-5bac-9ee1-73c64877f0d1', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 37, 37, 'A resistor is connected to a sinusoidal supply of peak 10 V and then to a 6.0 V d.c. supply. Calculate (mean a.c. power) ÷ (d.c. power).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.389', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P ∝ V²: ratio = (10 ÷ √2)² ÷ 6.0² = 50 ÷ 36 = 1.39. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: V_rms = 7.07 V. C1: ratio of squares. A1: ratio = 1.39.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgdb116713-t fgdb116713-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgdb116713-t">a.c. and d.c. supplies</title><desc id="fgdb116713-d">Graph of p.d. against time t: a sine curve of peak 10 V (the a.c. supply) and a horizontal dashed line at 6.0 V (the d.c. supply). Two periods are shown.</desc><line x1="36.2" y1="138" x2="388" y2="138" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="242" x2="36.2" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,138 385.7,141 385.7,135" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="36.2,24 39.1,30.3 33.2,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="36.2" y1="138" x2="36.2" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="36.2" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="209.1" y1="138" x2="209.1" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="209.1" y1="34" x2="209.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db