('8e86bc0e-5a69-5336-8e02-686a7911f0a8', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 42, 42, 'A 2.8 kW kettle runs on a 230 V r.m.s. supply. (a) Calculate the r.m.s. current. (b) Calculate the peak current. (c) Explain why a 13 A fuse is suitable even though the peak current is larger than 13 A. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '17.22', 'A', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) I_rms = 2800 ÷ 230 = 12.2 A. (b) I₀ = √2 × 12.17 = 17.2 A. (c) Fuses respond to heating, which depends on the r.m.s. current, 12.2 A, below 13 A. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: I = P/V. C1: × √2. C1: value. B1: heating depends on r.m.s. A1: I₀ = 17.2 A.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('5f4c6ee3-88c5-5f57-9aef-581fa12b6af8', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 43, 43, 'An oscilloscope shows a sinusoidal trace. The Y-gain is 5.0 V per division and the peak is 3.4 divisions above the centre line. The time-base is 2.0 ms per division and one cycle spans 5.0 divisions. (a) Calculate the peak voltage. (b) Calculate the r.m.s. voltage. (c) Calculate the frequency. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '12.02', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) V₀ = 3.4 × 5.0 = 17 V. (b) V_rms = 17 ÷ √2 = 12.0 V. (c) T = 5.0 × 2.0 = 10 ms, so f = 1 ÷ 0.010 = 100 Hz. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: divisions × Y-gain. C1: V_rms. C1: period from time-base. C1: f = 1/T. B1: reading taken from centre line. A1: V_rms = 12.0 V.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 338" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd95702b0-t fgd95702b0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd95702b0-t">Oscilloscope trace</title><desc id="fgd95702b0-d">An oscilloscope screen with a grid of 1 cm divisions. A sine wave has its peaks 3.4 divisions above the centre line and one cycle spans 5.0 divisions horizontally. Y-gain 5.0 V per division; time-base 2.0 ms per division.</desc><rect x="20" y="12" width="340" height="272" rx="6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="54" y1="12" x2="54" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88" y1="12" x2="88" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="122" y1="12" x2="122" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-li