327.7,255.5 328.5,254.1 329.4,252.6 330.2,251 331.1,249.3 332,247.5 332.8,245.6 333.6,243.6 334.5,241.5 335.4,239.3 336.2,237.1 337,234.7 337.9,232.3 338.8,229.7 339.6,227.1 340.5,224.4 341.3,221.7 342.1,218.9 343,215.9 343.9,213 344.7,209.9 345.5,206.8 346.4,203.7 347.2,200.5 348.1,197.2 349,193.9 349.8,190.6 350.6,187.2 351.5,183.7 352.4,180.3 353.2,176.7 354,173.2 354.9,169.7 355.8,166.1 356.6,162.5 357.5,158.9 358.3,155.3 359.1,151.6 360,148" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="20" y="302" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Y-gain: 5.0 V per division</text><text x="20" y="322" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">time-base: 2.0 ms per division</text></svg>', 'An oscilloscope screen with a grid of 1 cm divisions. A sine wave has its peaks 3.4 divisions above the centre line and one cycle spans 5.0 divisions horizontally. Y-gain 5.0 V per division; time-base 2.0 ms per division.'),
('a74452eb-3240-56da-848e-8e654de3e2b7', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 44, 44, 'A heating element is rated at 2.0 kW on a 230 V r.m.s. supply. (a) State the power on a 230 V d.c. supply. (b) Calculate the power on a sinusoidal supply of peak value 230 V. Give only the answer to (b), in kW.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1 kW', 'kW', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 2.0 kW: 230 V r.m.s. has the same heating effect as 230 V d.c. (b) V_rms = 230 ÷ √2, so P ∝ V² is halved: P = 2.0 ÷ 2 = 1.0 kW. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: r.m.s. equals d.c. equivalent. M1: P ∝ V_rms². C1: factor ½. C1: value. A1: P = 1.0 kW.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('b1f6fa94-c3c6-53ad-aa88-0da6d6daa5f7', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 45, 45, 'A 3.0 kW heater runs for 4.0 hours a day for 30 days. (a) Calculate the energy used, in kW h. (b) Calculate the energy in joules. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.296e9', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 3.0 × 4.0 × 30 = 360 kW h. (b) E = 3.0 × 10³ × 4.0 × 3600 × 30 = 1.296 × 10⁹ J. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: kW h. C1: hours to seconds. C1: value. B1: 1 kW h = 3.6 MJ. A1: E = 1.30 × 10⁹ J.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('20b5e9a7-1991-5cc1-a88c-6da2785e174f', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 46, 46, 'A half-wave rectified sinusoidal voltage of peak V₀ has an r.m.s. value of V₀/2. (a) Explain why this is less than V₀/√2. (b) Calculate the mean power it delivers to a 50 Ω resistor when V₀ = 20 V. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) One half of every cycle is missing, so the mean of V² is halved. (b) V_rms = 20 ÷ 2 = 10 V; P = 10² ÷ 50 = 2.0 W. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: half the cycles removed. C1: V_rms = 10 V. M1: P = V_rms²/R. C1: value. A1: P = 2.0 W.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg8f5dec19-t fg8f5dec19-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg8f5dec19-t">Half-wave rectified voltage</title><desc id="fg8f5dec19-d">Graph of voltage against time t: the positive half of each sine cycle, peak V₀, with zero voltage during the other half of each period T. Two periods are shown.</desc><line x1="28.7" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="28.7" y1="242" x2="28.7" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="28.7,24 31.7,30.3 25.8,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="28.7" y1="242" x2="28.7" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="28.7" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="205.4" y1="242" x2="20