('4f8d2119-b6b4-5458-bb0a-0a0dafabb727', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 47, 47, 'The current in a resistor is I = 4.0 sin(100πt), with I in A and t in s. (a) State the peak current and the frequency. (b) Calculate the r.m.s. current. (c) Calculate the mean power in a 5.0 Ω resistor. (d) Calculate the current at t = 2.5 ms. Give only the answer to (d).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.828', 'A', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) I₀ = 4.0 A; ω = 100π, so f = 50 Hz. (b) I_rms = 4.0 ÷ √2 = 2.83 A. (c) P = ½ × 4.0² × 5.0 = 40 W. (d) ωt = 100π × 2.5 × 10⁻³ = π/4 rad, which is 45°: I = 4.0 × sin 45° = 2.83 A. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: I₀ and f. C1: I_rms. C1: mean power. M1: ωt in degrees. C1: instantaneous value. A1: I = 2.83 A.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('c7382378-7460-5823-bfa2-3dbdd9977cfb', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 48, 48, 'The UK mains is 230 V r.m.s. and the North American mains is 120 V r.m.s. (a) Calculate both peak voltages. (b) Calculate (power in a resistor on UK mains) ÷ (power in the same resistor on North American mains). Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.674', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 230 × √2 = 325 V and 120 × √2 = 170 V. (b) P ∝ V_rms²: ratio = (230 ÷ 120)² = 3.67. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: peak values. M1: P ∝ V². C1: ratio. B1: r.m.s. values used. A1: ratio = 3.67.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('75c3445c-e5b3-571b-8a3e-5f69b75cf9d3', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 49, 49, '(a) Show that the mean power delivered to a resistor by a sinusoidal supply is ½V₀I₀. (b) Calculate the mean power when V₀ = 170 V and I₀ = 2.0 A. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '170', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) P = V_rms I_rms = (V₀/√2)(I₀/√2) = ½V₀I₀. (b) P = 0.5 × 170 × 2.0 = 170 W. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: use r.m.s. values. B1: ½V₀I₀ shown. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: P = 170 W.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgaf619b8e-t fgaf619b8e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgaf619b8e-t">Power on an a.c. supply</title><desc id="fgaf619b8e-d">Graph of the instantaneous power P = V₀I₀ sin² ωt against time t. P rises from 0 to a maximum of V₀I₀ and back to 0 twice in each period T; a dashed line marks the level ½V₀I₀ halfway up.</desc><line x1="48.2" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="48.2" y1="242" x2="48.2" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="48.2,24 51.1,30.3 45.2,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="48.2" y1="242" x2="48.2" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="48.2" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="215.1" y1="242" x2="215.1" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stro