('585a6054-1c33-51c9-973f-b628ce608a4b', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '521788f0-c0f7-5ff9-94e2-bd6a8cd8daac', 'a-level', '27.1', '9702 coursebook 27.1 · Alternating current and r.m.s. values', 50, 50, 'A current of 3.0 A flows for 0.010 s and is then zero for 0.030 s, repeating. (a) Calculate the fraction of each cycle for which the current flows. (b) Calculate the r.m.s. current. (c) Calculate the mean power in a 20 Ω resistor. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.5', 'A', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.010 ÷ 0.040 = 0.25. (b) Mean of I² = 0.25 × 3.0² = 2.25 A², so I_rms = √2.25 = 1.5 A. (c) P = 2.25 × 20 = 45 W. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: fraction. C1: mean of I². C1: square root. C1: P = I_rms²R. B1: r.m.s. not mean. A1: I_rms = 1.5 A.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgf1b051f0-t fgf1b051f0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgf1b051f0-t">Pulsed current</title><desc id="fgf1b051f0-d">Graph of current against time: 3.0 A from 0 to 0.010 s, then zero until 0.040 s, after which the pattern repeats (3.0 A from 0.040 s to 0.050 s, zero to 0.080 s).</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="113.5" y1="34" x2="113.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="203" y1="34" x2="203" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="292.5" y1="34" x2="292.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:no