('05c294aa-3ba7-58f0-b6b3-2424fd345d9a', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 20, 20, 'A sinusoidal voltage has a peak of 9.0 V. What is its peak-to-peak value?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '18', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'V_pp = 2 × 9.0 = 18 V. Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: V_pp = 18 V.', 1, NULL, NULL),
('0f503757-f1b5-592a-88c9-111bcafccb0c', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 21, 21, 'Which statement about a sinusoidal alternating voltage is correct?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The positive and negative half cycles have the same shape and size', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'A sine wave is symmetrical about the time axis. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (The positive and negative half cycles have the same shape and size).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('7f81c62a-f700-5120-a87c-08ecc8877a29', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 22, 22, 'An oscilloscope screen is 10 divisions wide, with the time-base at 2.0 ms per division. A 200 Hz signal is displayed. How many complete cycles appear?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Screen time = 10 × 2.0 = 20 ms. Cycles = 0.020 × 200 = 4.0. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: total time × f. A1: cycles = 4.0.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('cec51ab7-4667-598c-9dcc-88ab4917fdab', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 23, 23, 'A sinusoidal voltage of peak 20 V and frequency 50 Hz is zero at t = 0 and rising. Calculate the voltage at t = 3.0 ms.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '16.18', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'ωt = 2π × 50 × 3.0 × 10⁻³ = 0.942 rad, which is 54.0°. V = 20 × sin 54.0° = 16.2 V. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: ωt. C1: V = V₀ sin ωt. A1: V = 16.2 V.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4c6a58a9-t fg4c6a58a9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4c6a58a9-t">Sinusoidal voltage</title><desc id="fg4c6a58a9-d">Graph of voltage against time in ms for one 20 ms cycle of a sine wave of peak 20 V, starting at zero and rising. A dashed vertical line marks t = 3.0 ms.</desc><line x1="36.2" y1="34" x2="36.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="122.6" y1="34" x2="122.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="209.1" y1="34" x2="209.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="295.5" y1="34" x2="295.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="228.4" x2="382" y2="228.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="183.2" x2="382" y2="1