ound;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="20" y="370" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Y-gain: 2.0 V per division</text></svg>', 'An oscilloscope screen with a grid of divisions. A sine wave measures 8.4 divisions from crest to trough (4.2 divisions above and below the centre line). Y-gain 2.0 V per division.'),
('58f787d9-61aa-54b3-9409-b4b145007352', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 34, 34, 'Which equation describes a 50 Hz sinusoidal supply with an r.m.s. value of 230 V?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'V = 325 sin(314t)', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'V₀ = 230√2 = 325 V and ω = 2π × 50 = 314 rad s⁻¹. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: V₀ = √2 × 230. C1: ω = 2πf. C1: correct form. A1: D (V = 325 sin(314t)).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('42f54037-053b-5ad8-af39-6fda6a456f93', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 35, 35, 'For a sinusoidal voltage, calculate (instantaneous value) ÷ (peak value) when ωt = 60°.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.866', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'V/V₀ = sin 60° = 0.866. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: V/V₀ = sin ωt. C1: value. A1: ratio = 0.866.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('4cea6094-c41a-558a-b347-34b0c5836fbb', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 36, 36, 'Twelve complete cycles of a signal take 0.20 s. Calculate its frequency.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '60', 'Hz', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'f = 12 ÷ 0.20 = 60 Hz. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: cycles per second. C1: value. A1: f = 60 Hz.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('7e0b5a54-01ee-53f1-a05c-0d8571300462', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 37, 37, 'An alternating voltage is connected to an oscilloscope with the time-base switched off. What appears on the screen?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A vertical line whose length is the peak-to-peak voltage', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'With no horizontal sweep, the spot moves only up and down. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: no horizontal sweep. C1: line of length 2V₀. A1: B (A vertical line whose length is the peak-to-peak voltage).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('d056009f-74b5-54de-b728-a4f3e970d519', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 38, 38, 'For V = 15 sin(100πt), with V in volts and t in seconds, calculate the time at which V first reaches 10 V, in ms.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.323 ms', 'ms', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'sin(100πt) = 10 ÷ 15, so 100πt = sin⁻¹ 0.6667 = 41.8°, which is 0.730 rad. t = 0.7297 ÷ (100π) = 0.00232 s. In ms: 0.002323 × 1000 = 2.32. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: sin⁻¹. M1: angle in radians. C1: t. A1: t = 2.32 ms.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4d2bc79c-t fg4d2bc79c-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4d2bc79c-t">V = 15 sin(100πt)</title><desc id="fg4d2bc79c-d">Graph of V = 15 sin(100πt) against time in ms over one 20 ms cycle, peak 15 V. A dashed horizontal line marks V = 10 V.</desc><line x1="36.2" y1="34" x2="36.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="122.6" y1="34" x2="122.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="209.1" y1="34" x2="209.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="295.5" y1="34" x2="295.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="198.3" x2="382" y2="198.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="