('769c5898-db77-5231-93f3-faf8b000ad4f', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 39, 39, 'An oscilloscope with a Y-gain of 2.0 V per division and a time-base of 0.50 ms per division shows a sine wave with a peak-to-peak height of 7.0 divisions and 4.0 divisions per cycle. (a) Calculate the peak voltage. (b) Calculate the r.m.s. voltage. (c) Calculate the frequency. (d) Write the equation for the voltage in the form V = V₀ sin ωt. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '500', 'Hz', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) V₀ = 7.0 × 2.0 ÷ 2 = 7.0 V. (b) V_rms = 7.0 ÷ √2 = 4.95 V. (c) T = 4.0 × 0.50 = 2.0 ms, so f = 1 ÷ 2.0 × 10⁻³ = 500 Hz. (d) ω = 2π × 500 = 3140 rad s⁻¹, so V = 7.0 sin(3140t). Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: V₀. C1: V_rms. C1: T. C1: f. B1: equation with ω. A1: f = 500 Hz.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 338" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg649f2a2a-t fg649f2a2a-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg649f2a2a-t">Oscilloscope trace</title><desc id="fg649f2a2a-d">An oscilloscope screen with a grid of divisions. A sine wave measures 7.0 divisions from crest to trough and each cycle spans 4.0 divisions. Y-gain 2.0 V per division; time-base 0.50 ms per division.</desc><rect x="20" y="12" width="340" height="272" rx="6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="54" y1="12" x2="54" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88" y1="12" x2="88" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="122" y1="12" x2="122" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fi