('2b0985b9-7f40-5213-b054-9b34bccadb0a', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 41, 41, 'For a 50 Hz sinusoidal supply, (a) find the phase angles in the first half cycle at which |V| = 0.50V₀. (b) Hence find the fraction of each cycle for which |V| > 0.50V₀. (c) Calculate the total time per cycle for which |V| > 0.50V₀, in ms. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '13.33 ms', 'ms', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) sin θ = 0.50 at 30° and 150°. (b) |V| > 0.50V₀ from 30° to 150° in each half: 120° of every 180°, a fraction 120 ÷ 180 = 0.667. (c) Time = 0.6667 × 20 = 13.3 ms per 20 ms cycle. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: 30° and 150°. M1: same in negative half. C1: fraction. C1: × period. B1: period 20 ms. A1: t = 13.3 ms.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg49a01210-t fg49a01210-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg49a01210-t">Where |V| &gt; 0.50V₀</title><desc id="fg49a01210-d">Graph of a 50 Hz sinusoidal voltage of peak V₀ against time in ms over one 20 ms cycle. Dashed horizontal lines mark +0.50V₀ and −0.50V₀.</desc><line x1="59.2" y1="34" x2="59.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="139.9" y1="34" x2="139.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="220.6" y1="34" x2="220.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="301.3" y1="34" x2="301.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style=