08.1,197.9 309,196.1 309.9,194.2 310.7,192.2 311.5,190.1 312.4,188 313.2,185.8 314.1,183.5 315,181.2 315.8,178.9 316.6,176.5 317.5,174 318.4,171.5 319.2,169 320,166.5 320.9,163.9 321.8,161.3 322.6,158.6 323.5,156 324.3,153.3 325.1,150.7 326,148 326.9,145.3 327.7,142.7 328.5,140 329.4,137.4 330.2,134.7 331.1,132.1 332,129.5 332.8,127 333.6,124.5 334.5,122 335.4,119.5 336.2,117.1 337,114.8 337.9,112.5 338.8,110.2 339.6,108 340.5,105.9 341.3,103.8 342.1,101.8 343,99.9 343.9,98.1 344.7,96.3 345.5,94.6 346.4,93 347.2,91.5 348.1,90 349,88.7 349.8,87.4 350.6,86.2 351.5,85.2 352.4,84.2 353.2,83.3 354,82.6 354.9,81.9 355.8,81.3 356.6,80.8 357.5,80.5 358.3,80.2 359.1,80.1 360,80" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'An oscilloscope screen showing two sine waves, each with a cycle of 4.0 divisions. The peaks of the smaller trace are 1.0 division to the right of the peaks of the larger trace.'),
('e5397d63-fcf2-51c1-b141-fbdc52d9c129', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 43, 43, 'A neon lamp lights only when the p.d. across it is more than 200 V. It is connected to the 230 V r.m.s. mains. (a) Calculate the peak mains voltage. (b) Calculate the phase angle at which the lamp first lights in each half cycle. (c) Calculate the fraction of the time for which the lamp is lit. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.5784', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) V₀ = 230 × √2 = 325 V. (b) sin θ = 200 ÷ 325.3 = 0.6149, so θ = sin⁻¹ 0.6149 = 37.9°. (c) It is lit from θ to 180° − θ in each half: fraction = (180 − 2 × 37.94) ÷ 180 = 0.578. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: V₀. C1: sin⁻¹. M1: symmetric in each half. C1: fraction. B1: same for negative half. A1: fraction = 0.578.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1bac08c1-t fg1bac08c1-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1bac08c1-t">Neon lamp on the mains</title><desc id="fg1bac08c1-d">Graph of the 230 V r.m.s. mains p.d. against time t over one period T; its peak is √2 × 230 V. Dashed horizontal lines mark +200 V and −200 V: the lamp is lit while the p.d. is beyond these lines.</desc><line x1="42.9" y1="138" x2="388" y2="138" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42.9" y1="242" x2="42.9" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,138 385.7,141 385.7,135" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="42.9,24 45.8,30.3 39.9,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="42.9" y1="138" x2="42.9" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:no