('ba3b7ebe-8dcb-505b-886d-169d0d074e85', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 46, 46, 'A generator''s e.m.f. is E = 7.85 sin(157t), in volts. (a) Calculate its frequency. (b) Calculate the e.m.f. at t = 4.0 ms. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.612', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) f = 157 ÷ 2π = 25.0 Hz. (b) ωt = 157 × 4.0 × 10⁻³ = 0.628 rad, which is 36.0°: E = 7.85 × sin 36.0° = 4.61 V. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: f = ω/2π. C1: ωt. M1: in degrees. C1: value. A1: E = 4.61 V.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('7f29acc8-bef4-5856-a53a-ac8f731bb752', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 47, 47, 'A 10 Ω and a 30 Ω resistor in series are connected to a 12 V r.m.s. sinusoidal supply. An oscilloscope is connected across the 30 Ω resistor. (a) Calculate the r.m.s. p.d. across the 30 Ω resistor. (b) Calculate the peak p.d. across it. (c) Calculate the peak-to-peak p.d. shown on the oscilloscope. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '25.46', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) V = 12 × 30 ÷ 40 = 9.0 V. (b) V₀ = 9.0 × √2 = 12.7 V. (c) V_pp = 2 × 12.73 = 25.5 V. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: potential divider. C1: × √2. C1: × 2. B1: r.m.s. values divide like d.c. C1: value. A1: V_pp = 25.5 V.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 300 236" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1dbc5315-t fg1dbc5315-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1dbc5315-t">Potential divider on an a.c. supply</title><desc id="fg1dbc5315-d">Circuit: a 12 V r.m.s. a.c. supply in series with a 10 Ω resistor and a 30 Ω resistor. An oscilloscope is connected in parallel with the 30 Ω resistor.</desc><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="53.2" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="89.2" y1="48" x2="116.4" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="53.2" y="41" width="36" height="14" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="71.2" y="24" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10 Ω</text><line x1="116.4" y1="48" x2="132.4" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="258" y1="48" x2="274" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="132.4" y1="48" x2="132.4" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="258" y1="48" x2="258" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="132.4" y1="48" x2="177.2" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="213.2" y1="48" x2="258" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="177.2" y="41" width="36" height="14" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="195.2" y="24" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">30 Ω</text><line x1="132.4" y1="102" x2="175.2" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="215.2" y1="102" x2="258" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="175.2" y="89" width="40" height="26" rx="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M182.2,102 q3.25,-9 6.5,0 t6.5,0 t6.5,0 t6.5,0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="195.2" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">oscilloscope</text><circle cx="132.4" cy="48" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="258" cy="48" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="26" y1="196" x2="138" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="162" y1="196" x2="274" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="150" cy="196" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M143,196 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="220" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12 V r.m.s.</text><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="26" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="274" y1="48" x2="274" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Circuit: a 12 V r.m.s. a.c. supply in series with a 10 Ω resistor and a 30 Ω resistor. An oscilloscope is connected in parallel with the 30 Ω resistor.'),
('88bdb6c1-2a62-5e30-9339-2770d646b773', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 48, 48, 'Aircraft electrical systems use a 400 Hz supply. (a) Calculate the period. (b) Calculate the time taken for the voltage to rise from zero to its peak, in ms. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.625 ms', 'ms', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) T = 1 ÷ 400 = 2.5 × 10⁻³ s. (b) Zero to peak is a quarter cycle: 2.5 × 10⁻³ ÷ 4 = 6.25 × 10⁻⁴ s. In ms: 6.25 × 10⁻⁴ × 1000 = 0.625. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: T = 1/f. B1: quarter of a cycle. C1: value. C1: conversion. A1: t = 0.625 ms.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('a35c84d3-af17-5358-b56a-f951d3919d4e', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 49, 49, 'Two sinusoidal supplies of the same frequency, each of peak 10 V, are connected in series. (a) State the peak of their sum when they are in phase. (b) State it when they are 180° out of phase. (c) For a 90° phase difference, the peak of the sum is √(10² + 10²). Calculate it. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '14.14', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 20 V. (b) Zero: they cancel at every instant. (c) √(10² + 10²) = 14.1 V. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: in phase add. B1: antiphase cancel. C1: substitution. C1: value. M1: peaks not simultaneous for 90°. A1: V₀ = 14.1 V.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('6c214419-713e-537e-8c41-eb68f8441f05', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '1dcc934a-cbaa-4233-91fd-46dc3b235528', 'a-level', '27.2', '9702 coursebook 27.2 · Alternating voltages', 50, 50, 'The 230 V r.m.s. mains is displayed on an oscilloscope through a probe that divides the voltage by 10, with the Y-gain at 10 V per division. (a) Calculate the peak-to-peak mains voltage. (b) Calculate the peak-to-peak height of the trace in divisions. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6.505', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) V_pp = 2 × 230 × √2 = 651 V. (b) After the probe: 650.5 ÷ 10 = 65.1 V, so height = 65.05 ÷ 10 = 6.51 divisions. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: V_pp. C1: ÷ probe factor. C1: ÷ Y-gain. B1: fits on screen. A1: divisions = 6.51.', 5, NULL, NULL)
