('1bc25881-c298-52fa-bf6a-d4a93d857cb6', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '53ce2bac-1ccd-4752-8293-357079212398', 'a-level', '27.3', '9702 coursebook 27.3 · Power and alternating current', 43, 43, 'An electric shower draws 40 A r.m.s. from a 230 V r.m.s. supply. The cable has a total resistance of 0.10 Ω. (a) Calculate the power drawn from the supply. (b) Calculate the power wasted in the cable. (c) Calculate this as a percentage of the supply power. (d) Suggest why thick cables are used for showers. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '160', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) P = 230 × 40 = 9200 W. (b) P_cable = 40² × 0.10 = 160 W. (c) 160 ÷ 9200 × 100 = 1.74 %. (d) Thick cables have low resistance, so less heating at large currents. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: P = VI. C1: I²R. C1: percentage. B1: low resistance. C1: value. A1: P = 160 W.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 300 182" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg48c9f720-t fg48c9f720-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg48c9f720-t">Shower circuit</title><desc id="fg48c9f720-d">Circuit: a 230 V r.m.s. a.c. supply in series with the cable, of total resistance 0.10 Ω, the shower and an ammeter that reads 40 A r.m.s.</desc><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="60.7" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="96.7" y1="48" x2="131.4" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="60.7" y="41" width="36" height="14" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78.7" y="24" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">cable 0.10 Ω</text><line x1="131.4" y1="48" x2="149.8" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="185.8" y1="48" x2="204.2" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="149.8" y="41" width="36" height="14" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="167.8" y="24" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">shower</text><line x1="204.2" y1="48" x2="227.1" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="251.1" y1="48" x2="274" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="239.1" cy="48" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="239.1" y="48.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><line x1="26" y1="142" x2="138" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="162" y1="142" x2="274" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="150" cy="142" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M143,142 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="166" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">230 V r.m.s.</text><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="26" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="274" y1="48" x2="274" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Circuit: a 230 V r.m.s. a.c. supply in series with the cable, of total resistance 0.10 Ω, the shower and an ammeter that reads 40 A r.m.s.'),
('6edd8592-d4b6-5690-9012-7c6080428ca5', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '53ce2bac-1ccd-4752-8293-357079212398', 'a-level', '27.3', '9702 coursebook 27.3 · Power and alternating current', 44, 44, 'A 150 W refrigerator runs for 40 % of the time. (a) Calculate the energy it uses in one day, in kW h. (b) Calculate this in MJ. Give only the answer to (a).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.44', 'kW h', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) In kW and hours: E = 0.150 × 24 × 0.40 = 1.44 kW h. (b) 1.440 × 3.6 = 5.18 MJ. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: W to kW. C1: × 24 h × 0.40. C1: value. B1: 1 kW h = 3.6 MJ. A1: E = 1.44 kW h.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('b1f2cdbb-2158-5cc6-a9e3-7e3118579a82', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '53ce2bac-1ccd-4752-8293-357079212398', 'a-level', '27.3', '9702 coursebook 27.3 · Power and alternating current', 45, 45, 'A 40 Ω lamp is supplied through a single diode from a 230 V r.m.s. mains supply, so it receives only half of each cycle. (a) Calculate the mean power it would take with no diode. (b) Calculate the mean power with the diode. (c) Explain why the lamp flickers at 50 Hz. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '661.2', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) P = 230² ÷ 40 = 1320 W. (b) Only half the cycles deliver energy: P = 1322 ÷ 2 = 661 W. (c) It receives one pulse of power per cycle, 50 per second. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: full-wave power. M1: half the energy. C1: value. B1: one pulse per cycle. B1: flicker at 50 Hz. A1: P = 661 W.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 300 182" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd8b26a49-t fgd8b26a49-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd8b26a49-t">Lamp with a series diode</title><desc id="fgd8b26a49-d">Circuit: a 230 V r.m.s. mains supply in series with a diode and a 40 Ω lamp, so current flows in only one half of each cycle.</desc><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="79" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="48" x2="150" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="79,39 79,57 95,48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="39" x2="97" y2="57" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="95" y1="48" x2="97" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="48" x2="201" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="223" y1="48" x2="274" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="212" cy="48" r="11" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="204.2" y1="40.2" x2="219.8" y2="55.8" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="204.2" y1="55.8" x2="219.8" y2="40.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="212" y="24" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">40 Ω</text><line x1="26" y1="142" x2="138" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="162" y1="142" x2="274" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="150" cy="142" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M143,142 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="166" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">230 V r.m.s.</text><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="26" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="274" y1="48" x2="274" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Circuit: a 230 V r.m.s. mains supply in series with a diode and a 40 Ω lamp, so current flows in only one half of each cycle.'),
('bfe50aca-1fef-5ed4-91e9-6d4b16d9a658', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '53ce2bac-1ccd-4752-8293-357079212398', 'a-level', '27.3', '9702 coursebook 27.3 · Power and alternating current', 46, 46, 'A sinusoidal voltage and a square-wave voltage have the same peak value V₀ and are applied in turn to the same resistor. (a) State the r.m.s. value of each. (b) Calculate (mean power with square wave) ÷ (mean power with sine wave). Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Square wave: V₀. Sine wave: V₀/√2. (b) P ∝ V_rms²: ratio = V₀² ÷ (V₀²/2) = 2 × 1 = 2.0. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: square r.m.s. C1: sine r.m.s. M1: P ∝ V_rms². C1: ratio. A1: ratio = 2.0.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg7153ac96-t fg7153ac96-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg7153ac96-t">Sine and square waves</title><desc id="fg7153ac96-d">Graph against time t over two periods T of a sine wave (solid) and a square wave (dashed), both with peak value V₀: the square wave stays at +V₀ for half of each period and −V₀ for the other half.</desc><line x1="35.4" y1="138" x2="388" y2="138" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="35.4" y1="242" x2="35.4" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,138 385.7,141 385.7,135" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="35.4,24 38.4,30.3 32.5,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="35.4" y1="138" x2="35.4" y2="142" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="35.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="208.