('a97f2533-4945-5f13-b11f-8bda872ae4d5', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 16, 16, 'A bridge rectifier is fed with 12 V r.m.s. Two diodes, each with a forward p.d. of 0.70 V, conduct at a time. Calculate the peak output.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '15.57', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'V₀ = √2 × 12 − 2 × 0.70 = 15.6 V. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: subtract two diode drops. A1: V₀ = 15.6 V.', 2, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 456 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg3a689349-t fg3a689349-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg3a689349-t">Bridge rectifier</title><desc id="fg3a689349-d">Circuit: a 12 V r.m.s. a.c. supply connected to two opposite corners of a bridge of four diodes; the load resistor is connected between the other two corners (+ on the right, − on the left).</desc><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="227" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="200" x2="227" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="97" y2="108" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="132" x2="97" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="97" cy="120" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M90,120 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="77" y="120" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12 V r.m.s.</text><line x1=