('c8306818-5291-5678-b14a-ce432c2ea66f', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 20, 20, 'A 60 Hz supply is full-wave rectified. How many output peaks are there each second?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '120', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Two output peaks per input cycle: 2 × 60 = 120 peaks per second. Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: peaks = 120.', 1, NULL, NULL),
('a90f905e-da15-5240-a36c-d5a8f21b300f', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 21, 21, 'Why does a single-diode (half-wave) rectifier waste much of the supply?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It blocks the negative half of every cycle, so no energy is delivered for half the time', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Only one half cycle in two reaches the load. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (It blocks the negative half of every cycle, so no energy is delivered for half the time).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('ab63b92c-4c4b-59c3-8585-1231276d9121', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 22, 22, 'A 470 µF smoothing capacitor is charged to 15 V at a peak. Calculate the charge stored, in mC.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.05 mC', 'mC', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Q = CV = 470 × 10⁻⁶ × 15 = 0.00705 C. In mC: 0.007050 × 1000 = 7.05. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: Q = CV. A1: Q = 7.05 mC.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('b3260d37-ddc6-550c-8517-34330e456edf', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 23, 23, 'What is meant by ripple in the output of a smoothed rectifier?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The small variation in output voltage that remains after smoothing', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The capacitor discharges slightly between peaks. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (The small variation in output voltage that remains after smoothing).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('156050e7-3edf-5a4d-ba19-b853623c0571', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 24, 24, 'A smoothing circuit needs a time constant of 0.50 s with a 500 Ω load. Calculate the capacitance needed, in µF.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1000', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['0.001']::text[], 'C = τ/R = 0.50 ÷ 500 = 1.0 × 10⁻³ F. In µF: 1.0 × 10⁻³ × 10⁶ = 1000. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: C = τ/R. A1: C = 1000 µF.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('1b8f62cf-bc90-5ca1-891c-c06f5d7eae61', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 25, 25, 'A smoothed full-wave output has a peak of 15 V. Between peaks (0.010 s) the capacitor discharges through the load with RC = 0.50 s. Using ΔV ≈ V₀t/RC, estimate the ripple.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.3', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'ΔV ≈ 15 × 0.010 ÷ 0.50 = 0.30 V. Mark scheme (3 marks). M1: ΔV ≈ V₀t/RC. C1: value. A1: ΔV = 0.30 V.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1db7114e-t fg1db7114e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1db7114e-t">Smoothed output</title><desc id="fg1db7114e-d">Graph (y axis not starting at zero) of the smoothed output p.d. against time in ms: it rises to the 15 V peak, then falls exponentially with RC = 0.50 s for 0.010 s until the next peak. The fall ΔV is the ripple.</desc><line x1="41" y1="34" x2="41" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="145.9" y1="34" x2="145.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="250.8" y1="34" x2="250.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="355.8" y1="34" x2="355.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="41" y1="67.5" x2="382" y2="67.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="41" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round