('2994d944-e57b-5964-aa63-3f9edfb73776', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 27, 27, 'The load resistance across a smoothed rectifier is doubled, with the same capacitor. What happens to the ripple?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It roughly halves', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Doubling R doubles RC, so the capacitor discharges about half as much between peaks. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: RC doubles. C1: ΔV ∝ 1/RC. A1: C (It roughly halves).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 456 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg375a5531-t fg375a5531-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg375a5531-t">Smoothed bridge rectifier</title><desc id="fg375a5531-d">Circuit: an a.c. supply feeding a bridge of four diodes; a smoothing capacitor and the load resistor are connected in parallel across the output.</desc><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="227" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="200" x2="227" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="97" y2="108" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="132" x2="97" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="97" cy="120" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M90,120 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="227" y1="40" x2="256.1" y2="73.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap