('0a742640-ff33-5c48-aec3-486e6d285300', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 28, 28, 'A full-wave rectifier on a 50 Hz supply has a peak output of 12 V and feeds a 240 Ω load. Estimate the capacitance needed for a ripple of no more than 0.50 V, in µF, using ΔV ≈ It/C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1000', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['0.001']::text[], 'I ≈ 12 ÷ 240 = 0.050 A. C ≈ It/ΔV = 0.050 × 0.010 ÷ 0.50 = 1.0 × 10⁻³ F. In µF: 1.0 × 10⁻³ × 10⁶ = 1000. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: load current. M1: ΔQ = It = CΔV. C1: C. A1: C = 1000 µF.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 456 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg956d4ccf-t fg956d4ccf-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg956d4ccf-t">Smoothed rectifier</title><desc id="fg956d4ccf-d">Circuit: an a.c. supply feeding a full-wave bridge of four diodes; a smoothing capacitor C and the 240 Ω load are in parallel across the output.</desc><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="227" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="200" x2="227" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="97" y2="108" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="132" x2="97" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="97" cy="120" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M90,120 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="227" y1="40" x2="256