inejoin:round"/><line x1="196.6" y1="74.7" x2="197.3" y2="74" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="157" y1="120" x2="186.1" y2="153.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="197.9" y1="166.8" x2="227" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="192.8,147.3 179.3,159.2 196.6,165.3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="204" y1="160.1" x2="190.5" y2="171.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="196.6" y1="165.3" x2="197.3" y2="166" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="297" y1="120" x2="387" y2="120" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="157" y1="120" x2="157" y2="244" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="157" y1="244" x2="387" y2="244" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="334" y1="120" x2="334" y2="177" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="334" y1="187" x2="334" y2="244" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="322" y1="177" x2="346" y2="177" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="322" y1="187" x2="346" y2="187" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="314" y="182" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">C</text><circle cx="334" cy="120" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="334" cy="244" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="387" y1="120" x2="387" y2="164" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="387" y1="200" x2="387" y2="244" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="380" y="164" width="14" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="415" y="182" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">240 Ω</text><circle cx="227" cy="40" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="227" cy="200" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="157" cy="120" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="297" cy="120" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><text x="309" y="107" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+</text><text x="144" y="107" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">−</text></svg>', 'Circuit: an a.c. supply feeding a full-wave bridge of four diodes; a smoothing capacitor C and the 240 Ω load are in parallel across the output.'),
('6e7cca16-7862-5854-a10e-4727cffed00a', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 29, 29, 'A smoothed rectifier gives about 12 V across a 1.0 kΩ load. Calculate the load current, in mA.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '12 mA', 'mA', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'I = V/R = 12 ÷ 1000 = 0.012 A. In mA: 0.012 × 1000 = 12. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: I = V/R. C1: conversion. A1: I = 12 mA.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('3789e9b0-c897-528d-a236-a8194c382018', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 30, 30, 'With the same capacitor and load, how does the ripple from a full-wave rectifier compare with that from a half-wave rectifier?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It is about half as large, because the capacitor discharges for only half as long between peaks', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Full-wave peaks come every T/2 instead of every T. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: shorter discharge time. C1: smaller ripple. A1: A (It is about half as large, because the capacitor discharges for only half as long between peaks).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e56b5814-8321-53bb-8ee7-3dc945e96e91', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 31, 31, 'A 470 µF smoothing capacitor''s p.d. falls by 0.40 V between peaks. Calculate the charge it supplies to the load in that time, in µC.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '188 uC', 'µC', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'ΔQ = CΔV = 470 × 10⁻⁶ × 0.40 = 1.88 × 10⁻⁴ C. In µC: 1.88 × 10⁻⁴ × 10⁶ = 188. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: ΔQ = CΔV. C1: conversion. A1: ΔQ = 188 µC.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('d2c3b120-c710-5401-9368-a98fa1c0c4c9', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 32, 32, 'A 1000 µF smoothing capacitor''s p.d. falls from 15.0 V to 14.5 V between peaks. Calculate the energy it delivers to the load, in mJ.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.375 mJ', 'mJ', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'ΔW = ½C(V₁² − V₂²) = 0.5 × 1000 × 10⁻⁶ × (15.0² − 14.5²) = 0.00738 J. In mJ: 0.007375 × 1000 = 7.38. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: difference of ½CV². C1: substitution. C1: conversion. A1: ΔW = 7.38 mJ.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('36b3f5d9-2114-5fe7-8665-59d42fa18e16', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 33, 33, 'Which change would NOT reduce the ripple from a smoothed rectifier?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Using a lower-frequency a.c. supply', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'A lower frequency means longer gaps between peaks, so more discharge. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: larger C or R reduces ripple. C1: full-wave halves gap. C1: lower f increases gap. A1: D (Using a lower-frequency a.c. supply).', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 456 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg375a5531-t fg375a5531-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg375a5531-t">Smoothed bridge rectifier</title><desc id="fg375a5531-d">Circuit: an a.c. supply feeding a bridge of four diodes; a smoothing capacitor and the load resistor are connected in parallel across the output.</desc><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="227" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="200" x2="227" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="97" y2="108" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="132" x2="97" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="97" cy="120" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M90,120 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="227" y1="40" x2="256.1" y2="73.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-wi