120" x2="387" y2="164" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="387" y1="200" x2="387" y2="244" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="380" y="164" width="14" height="36" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="227" cy="40" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="227" cy="200" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="157" cy="120" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="297" cy="120" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><text x="309" y="107" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+</text><text x="144" y="107" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">−</text></svg>', 'Circuit: an a.c. supply feeding a bridge of four diodes; a smoothing capacitor and the load resistor are connected in parallel across the output.'),
('581c8755-2f6c-5d70-9a9b-0fe3d6737afc', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 34, 34, 'A 9.0 V r.m.s. supply feeds a bridge rectifier whose conducting diodes each drop 0.70 V. Calculate the peak output voltage.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '11.33', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'V₀ = √2 × 9.0 − 2 × 0.70 = 11.3 V. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: V₀ = √2 V_rms. C1: two diode drops. A1: V₀ = 11.3 V.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 456 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg76b694f9-t fg76b694f9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg76b694f9-t">Bridge rectifier</title><desc id="fg76b694f9-d">Circuit: a 9.0 V r.m.s. a.c. supply connected to two opposite corners of a bridge of four diodes, with the load between the other two corners.</desc><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="227" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="200" x2="227" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="97" y2="108" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="132" x2="97" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="97" cy="120" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M90,120 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="77" y="120" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">9.0 V r.m.s.</text><line x1="227" y1="40" x2="256.1" y2="73.2" style="stroke: