380.5,103.2 380.9,103.6 381.3,104 381.6,104.4 382,104.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="45.3" y1="232" x2="57.3" y2="226" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="45.3" y1="226" x2="57.3" y2="220" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Graph (y axis not starting at zero) of the smoothed output against time t: it rises to 15.0 V at each peak and falls to 14.4 V just before the next one.'),
('f888503b-e26a-5290-aa13-fa0771815b1c', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 41, 41, 'Which describes the smoothed output of a half-wave rectifier?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A sharp rise near each positive peak, followed by a slow fall for the rest of the cycle', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The capacitor charges near the peak and then discharges through the load. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: charge near peak. C1: slow exponential discharge. A1: A (A sharp rise near each positive peak, followed by a slow fall for the rest of the cycle).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('1168aa5c-a1fa-599c-add6-b06015a223e7', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 42, 42, 'A transformer gives 12 V r.m.s. to a bridge rectifier; two diodes, each dropping 0.70 V, conduct at a time. The output is smoothed by a 2200 µF capacitor and feeds a 100 Ω load. The supply is 50 Hz. (a) Calculate the peak output voltage. (b) Calculate the time constant. (c) Estimate the ripple using ΔV ≈ V₀t/RC. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.7078', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) V₀ = √2 × 12 − 1.4 = 15.6 V. (b) RC = 100 × 2200 × 10⁻⁶ = 0.22 s. (c) t = 0.010 s, so ΔV ≈ 15.57 × 0.010 ÷ 0.22 = 0.708 V. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: V₀ with diode drops. C1: RC. C1: t for full-wave. M1: ΔV ≈ V₀t/RC. C1: value. A1: ΔV = 0.708 V.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 456 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg52a07814-t fg52a07814-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg52a07814-t">Smoothed bridge rectifier</title><desc id="fg52a07814-d">Circuit: a 12 V r.m.s. supply from a transformer feeding a bridge of four diodes; a 2200 µF smoothing capacitor and a 100 Ω load are in parallel across the output.</desc><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="227" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="200" x2="227" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="97" y2="108" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="132" x2="97" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="97" cy="120" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke