('63a29847-85d6-5544-bd5a-079aeb12f9e3', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 43, 43, 'A half-wave rectifier on a 50 Hz supply has a smoothing capacitor charged to 10 V at each peak, with RC = 0.10 s. (a) State the time between peaks. (b) Calculate the p.d. just before the next peak. (c) Calculate the ripple. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.813', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.020 s. (b) V = 10 × e^(−0.020/0.10) = 8.19 V. (c) Ripple = 10 − 8.187 = 1.81 V. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: one peak per cycle. C1: V = V₀e^(−t/RC). C1: ripple. B1: approximation ΔV ≈ V₀t/RC gives 2.0 V. A1: ΔV = 1.81 V.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg75575625-t fg75575625-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg75575625-t">Smoothed half-wave output</title><desc id="fg75575625-d">Graph of p.d. against time in ms for a half-wave rectifier on 50 Hz. The dashed curve is the rectified supply, peak 10 V; the solid curve is the capacitor p.d., which decays with RC = 0.10 s for a whole 20 ms period between peaks.</desc><line x1="41" y1="34" x2="41" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="109.2" y1="34" x2="109.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="177.4" y1="34" x2="177.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="245.6" y1="34" x2="245.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="313.8" y1="34" x2="313.8" y2="242" style="st