('1b74c3a2-646e-535f-aca2-4521767e06ff', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 46, 46, 'A smoothed full-wave output on a 50 Hz supply rises to 14.0 V and falls to 13.2 V before each new peak. The load is 470 Ω. (a) State the ripple. (b) Estimate the mean load current. (c) Estimate the smoothing capacitance, in µF. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '361.7', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['3.617e-4']::text[], '(a) 14.0 − 13.2 = 0.80 V. (b) I ≈ 13.6 ÷ 470 = 0.0289 A. (c) C ≈ It/ΔV = 0.02894 × 0.010 ÷ 0.80 = 3.62 × 10⁻⁴ F. In µF: 3.617 × 10⁻⁴ × 10⁶ = 362. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: ripple. C1: mean voltage. C1: I = V/R. M1: C = It/ΔV. C1: value. A1: C = 362 µF.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1b7d7331-t fg1b7d7331-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1b7d7331-t">Smoothed output</title><desc id="fg1b7d7331-d">Graph (y axis not starting at zero) of the smoothed full-wave output on 50 Hz against time in ms: it rises to 14.0 V at each peak, 10 ms apart, and falls to 13.2 V just before the next one.</desc><line x1="51.3" y1="34" x2="51.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="117.4" y1="34" x2="117.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="183.6" y1="34" x2="183.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="249.7" y1="34" x2="249.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="315.9" y1="34" x2="315.9" y2="242" st