('a42b7458-931c-5850-a57f-8cc1535bc554', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 47, 47, 'A smoothed full-wave rectifier gives a ripple of 0.30 V. (a) Explain why the ripple would roughly double with half-wave rectification and the same capacitor and load. (b) State the expected ripple with half-wave rectification. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.6', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) With half-wave rectification the capacitor discharges for a whole period (20 ms) instead of half a period (10 ms) between peaks. (b) ΔV ≈ 2 × 0.30 = 0.60 V. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: discharge time doubled. M1: ΔV ∝ t. C1: factor 2. C1: value. A1: ΔV = 0.60 V.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('3093b260-6771-5103-a316-9c611697de11', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 48, 48, 'A smoothed supply gives a nearly steady 15 V across a 100 Ω load. (a) Calculate the load current. (b) Calculate the power delivered to the load. (c) The transformer supplies 2.6 W. Calculate the efficiency of the rectifier and smoothing circuit. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.25', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) I = 15 ÷ 100 = 0.15 A. (b) P = 15² ÷ 100 = 2.25 W. (c) Efficiency = 2.25 ÷ 2.6 × 100 = 86.5 %, the rest being lost mostly in the diodes. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: I = V/R. C1: P = V²/R. C1: efficiency. B1: losses in diodes. A1: P = 2.25 W.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('8935b6ff-5664-5141-b3fa-272b5cf53ad2', '94fd6e1e-0c0d-4097-b9f4-51457e7b9b07', '71ba01f7-9a9e-5018-974d-21999c276ce5', 'a-level', '27.4', '9702 coursebook 27.4 · Rectification and smoothing', 49, 49, 'A bridge rectifier is fed with 6.0 V r.m.s. Each diode has a forward p.d. of 0.70 V. (a) Explain why two diode drops must be subtracted. (b) Calculate the peak output voltage. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.085', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) In each half cycle, the current passes through two diodes in series with the load. (b) V₀ = √2 × 6.0 − 2 × 0.70 = 7.09 V. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: two diodes in each path. C1: √2 × 6.0. C1: subtract 1.4 V. C1: value. A1: V₀ = 7.09 V.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 456 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg5995e19c-t fg5995e19c-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg5995e19c-t">Bridge rectifier</title><desc id="fg5995e19c-d">Circuit: a 6.0 V r.m.s. a.c. supply connected to two opposite corners of a bridge of four diodes, with the load resistor between the other two corners.</desc><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="227" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="200" x2="227" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="40" x2="97" y2="108" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="97" y1="132" x2="97" y2="200" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="97" cy="120" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M90,120 q3.5,-7 7,0 t7,0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="77" y="120" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6.0 V r.m.s.</text><line x1="227" y1="40" x2="256.1" y2="73.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="267.9" y1="86.8" x2="297" y2="120" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="262.8,67.3 249.3,79.2 266.6,85.3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="274" y1="80.1" x2="260.5" y2="91.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266.6" y1="85.3" x2="267.3" y2="86" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="227" y1="200" x2="256.1" y2="166.8" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="267.9" y1="153.2" x2="297" y2="120" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="249.3,160.8 262.8,172.7 266.6,154.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="260.5" y1="148.1" x2="274" y2="159.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266.6" y1="154.7" x2="267.3" y2="154" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="157" y1="120" x2="186.1" y2="86.8" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="197.9" y1="73.2" x2="227" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="179.3,80.8 192.8,92.7 196.6,74.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2